From 0847fe5ae525d1079dd3e27b6a94f5861546d01d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:28:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] feat(spec): ship the adaptive-speculation tier configs
 in-tree

test_adaptive_wide.py resolves its two tier configs relative to
adaptive_spec_params.py, so they belong in the tree rather than in whatever
directory happened to hold them during development. QWENOPT_ADAPTIVE_CONFIG_DIR
overrides the location to test a hand-tuned pair.

adaptive_flashnext.json  -- 4 tiers; bs1 candidate steps [3, 5, 7].
adaptive_flashnext_lean.json -- VRAM-lean fallback; bs1 [3, 7], union {3,7} = 2
  runtime states and 9 batch-size captures, against 13 for the 4-state config
  and 8 for a static one. Boot this first if the 4-state config runs out of
  VRAM during graph capture.

Hysteresis in both is DERIVED, not tuned: for a slot whose candidates are
[.. c, next ..] the engine steps up when ema_accept_len > c - 0.5 +
up_hysteresis, so up_hysteresis = ema* - c + 0.5 places the step-up exactly at
the tok/s break-even ema*, and down_hysteresis places the step-down 0.25
ema-tokens below it. Re-derive after any change to the draft head.

Adaptive speculation stays OFF in every shipping configuration: it is the only
thing measured to raise accept length above 4.0, and it cost -3.8% throughput
and -67% of the KV pool.
